[5.822099, "o", "\u001b[1;37r\u001b[37S\u001b[1;1H\u001b[38;5;252m ▐▛███▜▌   Claude Code v2.1.220\r\n▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Bil\u001b[3;1H  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/proj\u001b[39m\u001b[4;1H\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel\r\n  event over an agent pane is served from\r\n  the fast client's local history overlay\r\n  rather than forwarded upstream. Point to\r\n  the exact implementation symbols and one\r\n  existing focused test that directly\r\n  asserts empty forwarded_input. Then\r\n  suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[14;1H\u001b[38;5;147m●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\r\n  railmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served\r\n  locally, not forwarded upstream:\r\n  1. handle_terminal_part gets the\r\n  SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to\r\n  LocalHistoryView.wheel.\r\n  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at;\r\n  a hit on an agent viewport scrolls\r\n  _HistoryViewport.offset and returns\r\n  HistoryAction with render_history=True and\r\n  forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\r\n  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream\r\n  when action.forwarded_input is set; empty\r\n  means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is\r\n  painted client-side via\r\n  surface.paint_overlays.\r\n  4. This is a fast-client history overlay\r\n  over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode;\r\n  the implementation notes stock tmux\r\n  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is\r\n\u001b[38;5;239m─────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b(B\u001b[m \r\n\u001b[38;5;239m─────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\u001b[38;5;244m  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ←\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[36;42H\u001b[38;5;244m for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[37;7H"]
[5.827945, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[H▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Bil\u001b[2;1H  ▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/proj\u001b[39m\u001b[3;1H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\r\n❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  event over an agent pane is served from\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  the fast client's local history overlay\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  rather than forwarded upstream. Point to\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  the exact implementation symbols and one\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  existing focused test that directly\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  asserts empty forwarded_input. Then\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\r\n  suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\r\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  railmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  1. handle_terminal_part gets the\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at;\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  a hit on an agent viewport scrolls\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  _HistoryViewport.offset and returns\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  HistoryAction with render_history=True and\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  when action.forwarded_input is set; empty\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  painted client-side via\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  surface.paint_overlays.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  4. This is a fast-client history overlay\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode;\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  the implementation notes stock tmux\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\r\n  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[1m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[1m\r\n❯\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;244m\r\n  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[48;5;70m\r\n[R]\u001b[30m[1][2] CC         \u001b[38;5;231m→ new session in railmux\u001b[30m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[37;7H"]
